          %p
            Similarly, as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+type+theory"} geometric type theory
            refers to a conjectural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+extension"} extension
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+logic"} geometric logic
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
            (under the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+category+theory+and+type+theory"} relation between category theory and type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            between them, a similar conjectural extension to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            corresponding to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            (and geometric morphisms between them) may deserve to be called
            %em geometric homotopy type theory
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+colimit"} preserved
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+images"} inverse images
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+%28infinity%2C1%29-theory"} essentially algebraic (infinity,1)-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pi-types"} Pi-types
          %p
            Traditionally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            in geometric homotopy type theory, hence the
            = succeed "," do
              %em geometric homotopy types
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            and maybe better as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} moduli ∞-stacks
